# Serve GPX with its registered media type.
#
# Apache has no built-in mapping for .gpx, so without this it sends no
# Content-Type header at all. The browser then sniffs the <?xml prolog every
# GPX starts with, decides the file is XML, and saves it as .xml - which
# Garmin Connect and Ride with GPS both refuse to import, since they filter
# uploads by extension. Chrome mostly gets it right because the download
# links carry a `download` attribute; Safari lets sniffing win.
#
# AddType needs AllowOverride FileInfo (or All) on this directory. With
# AllowOverride None this file is ignored harmlessly; if overrides are on but
# FileInfo is not granted, Apache returns 500 for the whole directory - so
# check the Content-Type after deploying, not just that the page loads.
AddType application/gpx+xml .gpx
